					</IRPYRawContainer>
				</Subjects>
			</IPropertyContainer>
			</_properties>
			<_rmmServerID type="a">-1</_rmmServerID>
			<m_type type="a">90</m_type>
			<m_pModelObject type="r">
				<IHandle type="e">
				</IHandle>
			</m_pModelObject>
			<m_pParent type="s">GUID 220d5967-b3ae-4b7e-b136-0a1cc02accf5</m_pParent>
			<m_name type="p">
				<CGIText type="e">
					<m_str type="a">EcuM will support%0D
%0D
1. FIXED Mode Management%0D
2. ECU modes recommended by Autosar - OFF, RUN, SLEEP%0D
3. STARTUP, WAKEUP, SHUTDOWN are other transient states supported inline with Autosar.%0D
4. Wakeup validation protocol.%0D
%0D
EcuM will not support:%0D
1. Flexible Mode Management%0D
%0D
Bsw Mode Management will not be used.%0D
Minimal Mandatory APIs which is required for EcuM will be supported for successful build%0D
%0D
User specific modes like abnormal voltage etc to be handled by respective SWC</m_str>
					<m_style type="a">Arial; 10 0 0 0 1 </m_style>
					<m_color type="p">
						<IColor type="e">
							<m_fgColor type="a">0</m_fgColor>
							<m_bgColor type="a">0</m_bgColor>
							<m_bgFlag type="a">0</m_bgFlag>
						</IColor>
					</m_color>
					<m_position type="a">1 0 0  </m_position>
					<m_nIdent type="a">0</m_nIdent>
					<m_bImplicitSetRectPoints type="a">0</m_bImplicitSetRectPoints>
					<m_nOrientationCtrlPt type="a">5</m_nOrientationCtrlPt>
				</CGIText>
			</m_name>
			<m_drawBehavior type="a">4096</m_drawBehavior>
			<m_transform type="a">0.365314 0 0 0.218978 504 83.3431 </m_transform>
			<m_bIsPreferencesInitialized type="a">1</m_bIsPreferencesInitialized>
			<m_AdditionalLabel type="p">
				<CGIText type="e">
					<m_style type="a">Arial; 10 0 0 0 1 </m_style>
					<m_color type="p">
						<IColor type="e">
							<m_fgColor type="a">0</m_fgColor>
							<m_bgColor type="a">0</m_bgColor>
							<m_bgFlag type="a">0</m_bgFlag>
						</IColor>
					</m_color>
					<m_position type="a">1 0 0  </m_position>
					<m_nIdent type="a">0</m_nIdent>
					<m_bImplicitSetRectPoints type="a">0</m_bImplicitSetRectPoints>
					<m_nOrientationCtrlPt type="a">1</m_nOrientationCtrlPt>
				</CGIText>
			</m_AdditionalLabel>
			<m_polygon type="a">4 0 3  0 1099  1084 1099  1084 3  </m_polygon>
			<m_nNameFormat type="a">0</m_nNameFormat>
			<m_nIsNameFormat type="a">0</m_nIsNameFormat>
			<_iTempdisplayTextFlag type="a">1</_iTempdisplayTextFlag>
			<m_bIsBoxStyle type="a">0</m_bIsBoxStyle>
			<m_pNoteText type="p"><IDescription type="e">
				<_textRTF type="a">{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fprq4\fcharset0 Tahoma;}}%0D
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\f0\fs16 EcuM will support\par%0D
\par%0D
1. FIXED Mode Management\par%0D
2. ECU modes recommended by \ulwave Autosar\ulnone  - OFF, RUN, SLEEP\par%0D
3. STARTUP, WAKEUP, SHUTDOWN are other transient states supported inline with \ulwave Autosar\ulnone .\par%0D
4. \ulwave Wakeup\ulnone  validation protocol.\par%0D
\par%0D
EcuM will not support:\par%0D
1. Flexible Mode Management\par%0D
\par%0D
\ulwave Bsw\ulnone  Mode Management will not be used.\par%0D
Minimal Mandatory APIs which is required for EcuM will be supported for successful build\par%0D
\par%0D
User specific modes like abnormal voltage etc to be handled by respective SWC\par%0D
}%0D
</_textRTF>
			</IDescription>
			</m_pNoteText>
		</CGIAnnotation>
